    "q-72722": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72722",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Suppose $B$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(B)=12.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}↔{R}_{2}$ (switching the second and the third rows). What is the value of $det(C)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-det(B) \\\\  & =-(12) \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
