    "q-130734": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130734",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Suppose $B$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(B)=120.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The row operation applied to $B$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{1}{8}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\frac{1}{8}det(B) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 120 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
