    "q-72728": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72728",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Suppose $X$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(X)=-60.$ The matrix $Y$ is obtained from $X$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(Y)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The row operation applied to $X$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =\\frac{1}{4}det(X) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-60) \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
